    "id": "i1",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     10,
     16
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests {@link BritishCutoverDate#until} returning a {@link ChronoPeriod} expressed in years, months, and days. The British cutover in September 1752 skips 11 days (Julian 2 Sep → Gregorian 14 Sep), so period calculations around that gap need special attention. Most expected values in the data provider are annotated with a comment that explains the arithmetic relative to the cutover gap."
   },
   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     19,
     25
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Provides (year1, month1, dom1, year2, month2, dom2, expectedYears, expectedMonths, expectedDays). <p>Start date = BritishCutoverDate.of(year1, month1, dom1) <br>End date = BritishCutoverDate.of(year2, month2, dom2) <br>Expected period returned by {@code start.until(end)}."
   },
